WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.372 --> 00:00:18.581
As and Priscilla headed toward their new home in Halifax, Priscilla's happy chatter cheered up Anne, helping her

2
00:00:18.621 --> 00:00:19.782
forget her homesickness.

3
00:00:19.802 --> 00:00:24.144
"The boardinghouse is a big, old-fashioned, stone house on St.

4
00:00:24.184 --> 00:00:26.005
John Street," said Priscilla.

5
00:00:26.025 --> 00:00:29.907
"Your bedroom is at the front and overlooks old St.

6
00:00:29.967 --> 00:00:30.988
John's graveyard."

7
00:00:32.864 --> 00:00:36.065
"That sounds gruesome," said Anne, shivering.

8
00:00:36.085 --> 00:00:39.646
"I think I'd prefer a room at the back of the house."

9
00:00:40.986 --> 00:00:43.107
"No, you wouldn't," replied Priscilla.

10
00:00:43.127 --> 00:00:47.748
"The graveyard is a lovely place, and besides, it's not used anymore.

11
00:00:48.508 --> 00:00:51.129
There are enormous trees and a big stone wall."

12
00:00:52.730 --> 00:00:57.191
Before Anne went to sleep in her new room that night, she went to the window and looked

13
00:00:57.311 --> 00:01:00.512
out. The moon was shining over the graveyard.

14
00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:06.243
"I suppose the same moon is shining down on Green Gables," she mused.

15
00:01:06.263 --> 00:01:08.305
"But I won't think about it.

16
00:01:09.105 --> 00:01:11.087
I'm not even going to have a good cry.

17
00:01:12.228 --> 00:01:14.689
I'll be sensible and go straight to sleep!"

18
00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:20.753
The next day Anne and Priscilla went to Redmond College and enrolled as students.

19
00:01:21.634 --> 00:01:23.595
Gilbert and Charlie were nowhere to be seen.

20
00:01:23.615 --> 00:01:29.479
"I never thought I'd be glad to see a Sloane," said Priscilla as they crossed the campus on

21
00:01:29.499 --> 00:01:30.020
the way home.

22
00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:34.422
"But I'd welcome Charlie's goggle eyes almost ecstatically.

23
00:01:35.543 --> 00:01:37.124
At least they'd be familiar eyes."

24
00:01:37.144 --> 00:01:39.165
"I know."

25
00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:40.426
Anne sighed.

26
00:01:41.347 --> 00:01:44.729
"I feel as insignificant as a leaf in a forest here."

27
00:01:44.749 --> 00:01:51.213
"Anne, did you notice the girl who stood alone all morning—the pretty one with the brown suit and

28
00:01:51.253 --> 00:01:51.813
pink hat?"

29
00:01:52.054 --> 00:01:52.894
Priscilla asked.

30
00:01:52.914 --> 00:01:55.476
"Yes," said Anne.

31
00:01:56.424 --> 00:02:01.226
"I noticed her particularly because she seemed as lonely and friendless as I felt.

32
00:02:02.046 --> 00:02:04.667
I had you, of course, but she had no one."

33
00:02:04.687 --> 00:02:10.150
"She looked as though she wanted to approach us, but she did not," added Priscilla.

34
00:02:12.370 --> 00:02:16.052
After lunch Anne asked Priscilla if she wanted to take a stroll through St.

35
00:02:16.092 --> 00:02:16.972
John's graveyard.

36
00:02:16.992 --> 00:02:22.915
"I don't know that a graveyard is a very good place to go to cheer myself up, but

37
00:02:22.975 --> 00:02:25.916
it has such beautiful trees," said Anne.

38
00:02:26.816 --> 00:02:30.959
"I'll sit and shut my eyes and imagine I'm in the Avonlea woods."

39
00:02:32.561 --> 00:02:36.183
But as they strolled through the graveyard, Anne couldn't stop looking around.

40
00:02:36.844 --> 00:02:39.185
She was fascinated by the old gravestones.

41
00:02:39.205 --> 00:02:45.630
"'Here lies the body of Albert Crawford,'" Anne read from a worn, gray slab.

42
00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:53.016
"'He was a brave officer, the best of husbands, the best of fathers, the best of friends.

43
00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:58.764
He died October 29, 1792, aged 84 years.'

44
00:02:59.965 --> 00:03:02.668
He must have led an adventurous life, Priscilla!"

45
00:03:02.688 --> 00:03:04.669
"Look, Anne."

46
00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:07.512
Priscilla gestured toward the end of the path.

47
00:03:07.532 --> 00:03:10.774
"It's the girl we saw at Redmond College this morning!

48
00:03:12.096 --> 00:03:13.036
I've been watching her.

49
00:03:14.057 --> 00:03:17.460
She has started to walk toward us and then turned back at least five times!

50
00:03:18.981 --> 00:03:20.222
Maybe she's very shy.

51
00:03:21.023 --> 00:03:21.844
Let's go and meet her."

52
00:03:23.092 --> 00:03:27.035
They walked toward the stranger, who was sitting under an enormous willow tree.

53
00:03:28.035 --> 00:03:33.919
She was certainly very pretty, and still wore the fashionable brown suit and a pale pink hat with

54
00:03:33.999 --> 00:03:34.800
brown poppies.

55
00:03:36.221 --> 00:03:41.424
Priscilla and Anne suddenly felt very self-conscious in their unfashionable clothes from the country.

56
00:03:42.185 --> 00:03:44.987
For a moment both girls felt like turning back.

57
00:03:46.148 --> 00:03:47.549
But it was too late to retreat.

58
00:03:48.149 --> 00:03:52.372
The girl sprang up and came forward with an outstretched hand and a friendly smile.

59
00:03:53.284 --> 00:03:55.105
"Oh, I've been dying to meet you girls.

60
00:03:55.805 --> 00:03:58.566
I saw you at Redmond this morning," she said eagerly.

61
00:03:58.586 --> 00:04:01.306
"Wasn't it awful there?

62
00:04:02.307 --> 00:04:04.847
I was wishing I had stayed home and gotten married instead!"

63
00:04:06.088 --> 00:04:09.008
Anne and Priscilla both laughed at this surprising comment.

64
00:04:09.669 --> 00:04:11.289
The brown-eyed girl laughed too.

65
00:04:11.309 --> 00:04:13.270
"Come," she said.

66
00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:15.530
"Let's sit down and get acquainted.

67
00:04:15.550 --> 00:04:20.312
I know we're going to be friends—I knew when I saw you at Redmond, and I wanted to

68
00:04:20.352 --> 00:04:21.312
come and say hello."

69
00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:24.141
"Why didn't you?"

70
00:04:24.621 --> 00:04:25.301
asked Priscilla.

71
00:04:25.321 --> 00:04:30.125
"Because I simply couldn't make up my mind," the girl said sorrowfully.

72
00:04:30.145 --> 00:04:33.067
"I can never make up my mind about anything."

73
00:04:33.087 --> 00:04:36.609
"We thought you were too shy," said Anne.

74
00:04:36.629 --> 00:04:38.150
"No, no.

75
00:04:38.411 --> 00:04:39.131
I'm not shy.

76
00:04:40.552 --> 00:04:42.934
My name's Philippa Gordon— Phil for short.

77
00:04:43.574 --> 00:04:44.135
Call me Phil."

78
00:04:44.155 --> 00:04:49.158
"She's Priscilla Grant," said Anne, pointing.

79
00:04:50.179 --> 00:04:53.906
"And she's Anne Shirley," said Priscilla, pointing in turn.

80
00:04:53.926 --> 00:04:57.989
"And we're from the island," said both together.

81
00:04:58.009 --> 00:05:01.732
"I'm from Bolingbroke, Nova Scotia," said Philippa.

82
00:05:01.752 --> 00:05:04.775
"Bolingbroke!" exclaimed Anne.

83
00:05:04.795 --> 00:05:06.997
"That's where I was born."

84
00:05:07.017 --> 00:05:10.600
"Well, we're old neighbors, aren't we?"

85
00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:11.660
Phil laughed.

86
00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:18.606
"I don't know how you made up your mind to come to Redmond at all if you are

87
00:05:18.646 --> 00:05:22.213
really such an indecisive person," said Priscilla, amused.

88
00:05:22.233 --> 00:05:23.834
"Oh, I didn't!

89
00:05:24.314 --> 00:05:26.075
My father wanted me to go to college.

90
00:05:27.236 --> 00:05:31.518
I have heaps of brains," Phil chatted, "but it's such hard work to use them.

91
00:05:32.459 --> 00:05:35.040
My mother wanted me to get married, but I'm too young!

92
00:05:36.181 --> 00:05:39.043
Besides, how could I ever decide which man to marry?"

93
00:05:39.063 --> 00:05:42.184
"Were there so many?"

94
00:05:42.565 --> 00:05:43.185
Anne laughed.

95
00:05:44.146 --> 00:05:47.928
"Heaps. Boys like me a lot—they really do.

96
00:05:48.864 --> 00:05:53.208
But there were only two boys that mattered—Alec and Alonzo.

97
00:05:53.988 --> 00:05:55.750
The rest were all too young or too poor."

98
00:05:55.770 --> 00:05:58.432
"Do you love either of them?"

99
00:05:58.852 --> 00:05:59.433
asked Anne.

100
00:05:59.453 --> 00:06:03.095
"Oh no, I couldn't love anybody!"

101
00:06:03.516 --> 00:06:04.096
said Phil.

102
00:06:04.116 --> 00:06:08.300
"Being in love makes you a perfect slave, I think!

103
00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:12.123
I saw one handsome fellow this morning, though.

104
00:06:12.943 --> 00:06:14.344
His friend called him Gilbert."

105
00:06:15.345 --> 00:06:18.548
Anne felt a prick of annoyance and decided it was time to leave.

106
00:06:19.392 --> 00:06:20.213
"Don't go yet!"

107
00:06:20.573 --> 00:06:21.154
Phil said.

108
00:06:21.174 --> 00:06:22.855
"Let's meet tomorrow!"

109
00:06:23.957 --> 00:06:29.322
Anne and Priscilla could not resist Phil's cheerfulness and made plans to meet their first new friend again

110
00:06:29.342 --> 00:06:30.062
the next day.
